// The brick houses are pinned to the ground. Each wooden house and tree hangs
// on a hinge to its nearest brick house, which also keeps it from merging into
// the terrain while it waits; the hinge breaks when the water lifts it.
pin 2 2231 1917
pin 6 2526 1897
joint 0 2 2178 1906 hinge 2000
joint 1 2 2203 1912 hinge 2000
joint 3 2 2259 1919 hinge 2000
joint 4 2 2288 1918 hinge 2000
joint 5 6 2500 1906 hinge 2000
joint 7 6 2555 1884 hinge 2000
joint 8 6 2583 1870 hinge 2000

[events]
// Charges set in the water against the foot of the dam go off at tick 1. Set
// upstream of the concrete and small enough not to reach the air beyond it,
// they throw the concrete out into the valley as rubble and spray instead of
// back into the reservoir, and light no fire for the flood to trap. The dam is
// then gone; no water is deleted.
at 1: explode 2040 1600 24 220
at 1: explode 2040 1750 24 220
at 1: explode 2040 1880 24 220
at 1: fill 2048 0 2056 2000 air

